lens:
Trust and consumer law, round 6: a first-time Indian shopper (28, Pune, buys on Instagram, burnt by fake jewellery sites) and a reviewer who knows the CCPA 2023 dark-pattern guidelines, the Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) Rules 2020 (Naira sells its own stock, so the inventory-entity duties in r.7 apply), BIS IS 19000:2022 and ASCI's influencer rules.

G3 passes. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_1-5.jpg and measure.json (06:59:17-21) are newer than prototype.html (06:58:55, md5 74dcaeee...), and my renders of an untouched copy agree: H1 399-427, facts end 562, bar 575, no console errors. fold.png is md5-identical to round 5's (d4ae18d6...), and fold-ad.png equals it by design (prism_sugar_p1 carries no confirmed angle).

G1 does not trip. The grep over page text, alt text, aria labels, title, meta description and JSON-LD hits only allowed text (probe.json 'hits'). All nine of my round-5 fixes landed, on the page or in the notes:
- the arm-A strings in build note 1;
- the four-link footer;
- the Instagram owner item and build note 10;
- the #jewellery build note 11, with a wider blocker 3;
- the damaged, wrong or missing owner item;
- the strike as launch blocker 5;
- 'Business address' under Reviews, with the seller-details owner item;
- the short policy line under Secure checkout;
- the UPI payee and courier sender item.

What is new this round sits one tap off the page. Round 5's 'Business address' and 'Contact & business address' links send her to /contact, which the Instagram browser titles 'Contact Naira Flore | Nashik Atelier & WhatsApp Support'. That page's footer (also on the policy, privacy and terms pages) says 'Demi-fine jewellery, 18K gold coated and crafted in Nashik'. Those are the Never-list claims in other words, and nothing in FACTS supports an origin. The delivery FAQ also says '3-7 working days' against this page's 3-5. Nothing in the build notes or their test reaches these pages. The other gaps the law names are how a faulty piece gets back and who pays, and whether she can cancel before dispatch.

Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/r6trust:
- probe.js and probe.json: strings, the G1 grep, fold geometry, a 12 s overlay watch, Buy now, the bag at 1, 2 and 4 pieces, the bag's policy opened in place, the policy fold, the footer, a Riya landing with the viewer, 320/412/360x560 fact lines;
- bag1.png, bag1_pol.png, bag2.png, bag4.png, hand.png, policy.png, land_riya.png, viewer_clip.png, size.png;
- foot.js, foot.json, foot2.js and foot2.json: candidate wordings for the bag's short policy line, measured at 320 (11px) and 360 (12px) on the copy at runtime. The prototype was not edited.
The repo was checked at origin/main bd412960: Footer.tsx, ContactUs.tsx, FounderStoryTeaser.tsx, FAQs.tsx, ExchangeReturnPolicy.tsx, TermsOfService.tsx, App.tsx (PieceRoute renders JewelDetailNext with Footer compact slim), serviceability.ts, promo.ts and fastrr.ts.

score_now is the weighted mean of the same 16 criteria as rounds 4 and 5: 654.2 / 74 = 8.84, reported as 8.8. The critique is also written to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/pdp10/rounds/r6_trust.json.

roadmap:
